<description>&lt;p&gt;Lawmakers have opened Venezuela's crisis-hit power sector to private investment, shifting from previous state control, while Brazil and Venezuela have agreed to upgrade ties through oil investment talks and Fluor has returned to the country after a two-decade hiatus. The United States managed $12 billion in Venezuelan oil revenue and secret talks involving a Trump aide have been linked to Vitol's win in crude sales rights. Delcy Rodríguez and Lula da Silva have pledged to fully reactivate bilateral ties, and Conviasa will resume flights to Cuba despite fuel shortages on the island. The conflict environment still records 2 battle-related deaths in 2007, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiswFBVV95cUxPUFlIb29ycnNCZUxoSEVHSWk3dENoZ0VqOXlkZ0l5NDQyQ01mdzFWbU9SZlBxUzc2dFc1eW5NRkRVUURMRElabEZ2UTJkQ0hzSU5vY0Vnanhab09LWFJQVDVlR0Z0WFdnSElfVUdKMjN4MzQ3aHVhTkJFYU83OUl6X1pQcGdtaTJZQkxTUElfLVZRYVJRSEZET19PNktaY3JEZVB4TUltNEZEMWJZck40RTlzSQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMirwFBVV95cUxNN3k3UW9kdVl5bC1vS2g4ZWdKd1luSGp3WThza3dJcmR0WGx4ckpmeTh5N1pCLTRCT0hwQWJoSmlfM2luQXctRzIxRmdQNVZsUjJkU1QyZmwtZlAxUXplejZBaV9aN2Zqb3NUb0pKX1REb2lYMFBMZk9GNjRFWHV1VXdGS1hvSnBDamJrbHhQQ0FTbVYxdlZMNDRYUV9pRkpBendkZ05JRTc5dlJyTEdn?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiswFBVV95cUxNcUI1X09sR3JkQkU4ODhvc0NPY0t2X1VzQlRLVXdmMFJldm5FX1BCOU1HR05Ta0sxUnk1TGRZbEpoNEp3WE1Ca3Y1ZHYxR1FVQThEU3EzZmxpOE94TEFsYm80cDZJd1ZFYzF0QXVNdmJsdjBhb25sYTZUbzFOYlgyb2Jsb29BQ2VqMmNfQ2VNNlNMQzV5b1ZLZndrR1plZlYyY1g5eXZvaFY3UnY3c3JkUXVHSQ?oc=5&quot;&gt;Bloomberg.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMivAFBVV95cUxOY01UNlVSYm43NkhaRFIzMEI1bVpkY0FORzUtS0YtRHAtQ2c3N0s1NzVhdkozaHZsWVo1dkRWU